BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cross-country-2@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260916T160000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Cross Country at Salem
LOCATION:Winter Island\, Salem
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nBoys: won 28–29\nGirls: won 20–35\
 nA sweep\, and a one-point thriller on the boys side. Marcus Morais won th
 e race in 19:20 as the Falcons edged Salem 28–29 for the boys' first dua
 l-meet win since 2024. Grace Conklin (23:01) and Madyson Danish (23:02) cr
 ossed a second apart to go 1–2 and lead the girls to a 20–35 win.\nSch
 edule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/sched
 ule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cross-country-3@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260923T163000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Cross Country vs Swampscott
LOCATION:Danvers High School
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nBoys: lost 45–17\nGirls: lost 33–2
 4\nSwampscott took both races\, but the Falcons ran fast on the home cours
 e: Marcus Morais dropped to 17:12 and Grace Conklin to 18:51\, each about 
 40 seconds quicker than they ran on the same course two weeks earlier.\nSc
 hedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/sche
 dule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cross-country-4@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260930T163000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Cross Country vs Saugus/Winthrop
LOCATION:Danvers High School
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nBoys: won 22–30\nGirls: won 16–40\
 nBoth squads got back to .500. Madyson Danish won the girls race and four 
 more Falcons followed her into the scoring in a 16–40 rout\, and the boy
 s won 22–30.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/
 cross-country/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cross-country-5@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T170000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Cross Country: MSTCA Bay State Invitational
LOCATION:Wrentham Developmental Center
DESCRIPTION:Invitational\nBoys: Marcus Morais\, 83 in 18:00.4\nGirls: Grace
  Conklin\, 15 in 19:46.7\nUnder the lights at the MSTCA's Twilight Meet\, 
 Grace Conklin ran 19:46.7 to finish 15th in the Varsity A race — the fif
 th-fastest 5K by a Danvers girl on athletic.net's all-time list. Marcus Mo
 rais led the boys in a personal-best 18:00.4\, one of four Falcon boys to 
 set a 5K best.\nSchedule and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/
 cross-country/schedule.html
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cross-country-6@danversfalconsathletics.org
DTSTAMP:20260801T000000Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261007T160000
DURATION:PT2H
SUMMARY:Danvers Cross Country at Marblehead
LOCATION:Lead Mills Conservation Area\, Marblehead
DESCRIPTION:Northeastern Conference\nBoys: lost 43–19\nGirls: lost 42–1
 9\nMarblehead swept both races at Lead Mills on the Magicians' senior day\
 , winning the boys meet 19–43 and the girls meet 19–42. Marcus Morais 
 split the Marblehead pack in second (18:14)\, and Grace Conklin (20:17) an
 d Madyson Danish (21:25) were third and sixth in the girls race.\nSchedule
  and results: https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.h
 tml
URL:https://danversfalconsathletics.org/cross-country/schedule.html
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
